# Fixed 2026-09-29, defect 131's class, lane X1. Symptom: a `{` alone on the
# line below its head, Allman's style, cost under a declaration the `{`'s
# report as the missing body and then `expected_declaration` at the `{`, at
# the `}` and at the body's lines between them, read as lines of the top
# level; under an `if` in a body the braces were read as a map literal, whose
# `:` each line then owed, and the `else` below them was refused. Cause: the habit was read only where its `{` ends
# the head's own line, and `fixedbugs-131-the-brace-habit-is-one-mistake`
# said so. A `{` alone on the line below a head whose line ended, past blank
# and comment lines, is now the habit too (`parse/brace_habit.ending`): named
# once, as the missing body it stands for, and its body read.

function main()
{  #~ missing_body
    x = 1
    if x == 1
    {  #~ missing_body
        y = 3 4  #~ expected_end_of_line
    }
    else
    {  #~ missing_body
        print(2)
    }
}

test "adds"
# the case
{  #~ missing_body
    assert 1 + 1 == 2
}

constant LIMIT: i64
{  #~ missing_body
    5
}
